From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Johannes Stein <johannesstein@freeze-dev.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 19:01:36 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 08/78] is_range_test: a constant on the left of the second
 comparison swaps that comparison

The noder branch set swapl instead of swapr, so for '(c1 >= x) and
(c2 >= x)' (or with <=) the second comparison kept its unswapped
direction, the 'two different bounds' check passed and the expression
became the range test c2 <= x <= c1. Found while reviewing the fix for
the constant-folding range-test bug.
---
 compiler/nadd.pas | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/compiler/nadd.pas b/compiler/nadd.pas
index 8d77d9ed..aa650ec3 100644
--- a/compiler/nadd.pas
+++ b/compiler/nadd.pas
@@ -440,7 +440,7 @@ const
 
           if noder.left.nodetype=ordconstn then
             begin
-              swapl:=true;
+              swapr:=true;
               cr:=tordconstnode(noder.left).value;
               valuer:=noder.right;
             end
